{"author":{"id":"8d7a7fea5b07a0d5d081edd516d55afeb51ce9c18b2b2be6ceb30eb17cd9b547"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794382234,"nonce":"1xei4ZnOM6kEJD5bdn8lnMj/12w=","message":"Review found a deadlock in the first version of the fix: DataSignals released its signals in Drop with dispose_signal, which takes the global graph lock. When the last clone of the data was held by a computed or effect closure, the drop happened while the graph disposed that closure, under the lock already held on the same thread, so the second lock hung (blinc_core probe: a computed holding the last clone, then Owner::dispose; blinc_layout probe: an effect holding TextInputData). The pattern exists in Blinc (time_picker, select, time_picker_wheel, color_picker, number_input, input_otp) and in fs-components view/editor.rs. Not present at the base commit, where the data had no Drop. Fix: the graph keeps the nodes a disposal removes (dispose_signal, dispose_derived, dispose_effect) and the callers drop them after releasing the lock. Tests: blinc_core/tests/data_signals.rs (computed and effect holding the last clone, a watchdog turns a hang into a failure; the live signal count of the graph is the same after 1000 rebuilds), blinc_layout (effect/computed holding TextInputData, computed holding ScrollRef). Both hang tests fail on the unfixed graph. Also checked: cargo check for x86_64-pc-windows-gnu (blinc_core, blinc_layout, blinc_cn) and blinc_app with wayland-frame-gate.","files":null}]}